---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import FaqOverlay from "../components/FaqOverlay.astro";
import CookieBanner from "../components/CookieBanner.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
    <CookieBanner />
    <FaqOverlay />
    <Header />

    <main class="page-wrapper">
        <!-- HERO -->
        <section class="hero-section">
            <div class="hero-container">
                <div class="hero-left-column">
                    <img
                        class="top-view-jaguar"
                        src="/images/jaguar-dtype-02.png"
                        alt="Jaguar car top view"
                        width="1199"
                        height="2133"
                        fetchpriority="high"
                        srcset="/images/jaguar-dtype-02-p-500.png 500w, /images/jaguar-dtype-02.png 640w"
                    />
                </div>
                <div class="hero-right-column">
                    <h1 class="h1">
                        Stop<br />
                        Boring!<br />Rev up <span>Wowing!</span>
                    </h1>
                    <div class="outline-block">
                        <h2 class="subtitle">
                            SHIFT INTO HIGH GEAR WITH OUR WOW
                        </h2>
                        <h3 class="subtitle-2">
                            <strong class="bold-text-11"
                                >Presentation &amp; Training
                            </strong>
                            <br />
                            <strong class="bold-text-111"
                                >Development Consultancy</strong
                            >
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="date-block">
                        <h2 class="date">
                            ACCELERATE YOUR STRATEGY EXECUTION DON'T BE PART OF
                            THE 80%...
                        </h2>
                    </div>
                    <div class="graphic-element-01"></div>
                    <div class="graphic-element-02"></div>
                    <div class="graphic-element-03"></div>
                    <div class="graphic-element-04"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SPEED BUMPS -->
        <section class="section-2 margin-top-220">
            <div class="container">
                <h2 class="heading-4">
                    KEEP READING IF YOU'RE FACING THESE SPEED BUMPS
                </h2>
                <p class="paragraph-2 bold-text-13">
                    <span class="metafora">
                        Imagine your business as a sleek sports car, primed for
                        a thrilling drive to success. Yet, as you hit the
                        accelerator, you encounter not just one, but several
                        unexpected roadblocks—like a flat tyre, engine trouble,
                        and a mysterious rattling sound—hindering your journey
                        forward.
                    </span>
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    <strong class="bold-text-13">
                        Every year, organisations spend over $30 billion on
                        strategy creation.
                        <strong>
                            The shocking reality? 80% of those strategies
                            fail—not because they're flawed, but because
                            execution breaks down.
                        </strong>
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        The road to success isn't just about crafting the perfect
                        plan; it's about ensuring <strong
                            >alignment, clarity, and action
                        </strong>at every level of the organisation. Execution
                        fails when teams
                        <strong>
                            lack clear communication, struggle to adopt change,
                            or don't have the resources to act effectively.
                        </strong>
                        <br />
                        <br />
                        At Wow Deck, we bridge the gap between strategy and execution
                        by tackling two of the most common <strong
                            >execution barriers:</strong
                        >
                    </strong>
                </p>
                <div class="div-block-14">
                    <img
                        class="car-drawing"
                        src="/images/car-tyres_v2.png"
                        alt="Car tyres drawing"
                        loading="lazy"
                        width="1200"
                        height="866"
                        srcset="/images/car-tyres_v2-p-500.png 500w, /images/car-tyres_v2.png 539w"
                    />
                </div>
                <div
                    class="accordion accordion-flush"
                    id="accordionFlushExample"
                >
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button
                                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#flush-collapseOne"
                                aria-expanded="false"
                                aria-controls="flush-collapseOne"
                            >
                                INEFFECTIVE BUSINESS COLLATERAL
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div
                            id="flush-collapseOne"
                            class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                            aria-labelledby="flush-headingOne"
                            data-bs-parent="#accordionFlushExample"
                        >
                            <p class="accordion-body">
                                Did you know that<br /><br />
                                71% of senior business technology decision-makers
                                are disappointed with B2B marketing content<sup
                                    >0</sup
                                >
                                <br /><br />
                                70% of your marketing materials are currently unused
                                by your sales team<sup>1</sup>
                                <br /><br />
                                Salespeople spend an astonishing 30 hours a month
                                searching for or creating their own content<sup
                                    >2</sup
                                >
                                <br /><br />
                                Approximate 64% of your sales team's precious time,
                                is burned in non-selling activities<sup>3</sup>
                                <br /><br />
                                Shockingly, 77% of B2B sales and marketing teams are
                                not aligned
                                <sup>4</sup>
                                <br /><br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://martechmap.com/"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >
                                    <sup>0</sup>Marketing Insights<br />
                                </a>
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.forrester.com/blogs/its-not-content-its-a-lack-of-buyer-insights-thats-the-problem/?ref_search=0_1694871258569"
                                    target="_blank"><sup>1</sup>Forrester®</a
                                >
                                <br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://seismic.com/blog/7-alarming-sales-performance-stats/"
                                    target="_blank"><sup>2</sup>Seismic</a
                                ><br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/kenkrogue/2018/01/10/why-sales-reps-spend-less-than-36-of-time-selling-and-less-than-18-in-crm/"
                                    target="_blank"><sup>3</sup>Forbes<br /></a
                                >
                                <a
                                    href="https://blog.hubspot.com/sales/hubspot-sales-strategy-report"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >
                                    <sup>4</sup>HubSpot<br /><br /></a
                                >
                                While direct studies on the similarity of marketing
                                and sales collateral within specific sectors might
                                be limited, related research consistently emphasizes
                                the challenges and importance of differentiation.
                                <br />
                                <br />
                                Reports from organizations such as
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.millerheimangroup.com/cso-insights"
                                    target="_blank"
                                    >CSO
                                </a>Insights and
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.gartner.com/en"
                                    target="_blank"
                                    >Gartner
                                </a>
                                that many presentations are perceived as too similar
                                and lack unique value propositions.
                                <br />
                                <br />
                                This underscores the broader necessity for presentations,
                                regardless of sector, to differentiate themselves
                                effectively. Often, if not all the time, solutions
                                including AI platforms, tend to follow existing models
                                rather than innovate beyond established norms.
                                <br />
                                <br />
                                So, unfortunately, many companies fail to BeUniqueLookUnique,
                                potentially missing out on valuable business opportunities.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button
                                class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#flush-collapseTwo"
                                aria-expanded="false"
                                aria-controls="flush-collapseTwo"
                            >
                                INEFFICIENT TRAINING PROGRAMS
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div
                            id="flush-collapseTwo"
                            class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                            aria-labelledby="flush-headingTwo"
                            data-bs-parent="#accordionFlushExample"
                        >
                            <p class="accordion-body">
                                The traditional training status quo often
                                overlooks several crucial aspects <br /><br
                                />First, training should align with business
                                needs and start with business metrics that
                                highlight specific problems<sup>1</sup>;
                                however, most stakeholders requesting training
                                cannot articulate clear and quantified training
                                objectives, such as "x to y by when", that need
                                to be improved<sup>2 - 3</sup>. <br /><br
                                />Second, training should address the root
                                causes of employee performance issues, such as
                                skills, motivation, knowledge, procedures,
                                tools, organizational culture, and environment<sup
                                    >1</sup
                                >. Most cases fail to prioritize and perform an
                                effective root cause analysis where all
                                stakeholders are fully involved before
                                developing any sort of solution<sup>3</sup>. <br
                                /><br />
                                Third, traditional training programs often fail to
                                emphasize lead metrics and accountability, mistakenly
                                believing that "training" alone can solve everything<sup
                                    >1</sup
                                >. Training is only part of a broader, holistic
                                solution<sup>3</sup>.
                                <br /><br />
                                Moreover, many training methods lack engagement and
                                relevance
                                <sup>4-5</sup>. They often miss hands-on
                                activities directly related to job tasks and
                                rely on outdated, uninspiring materials that
                                lead to disengagement and poor retention
                                <sup>3</sup>. <br /><br />
                                Finally, inadequate follow-up and coaching further
                                exacerbate these issues
                                <sup>6-7</sup>. <br /><br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.cathy-moore.com/"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >
                                    <sup>1</sup>Cathy Moore's action mapping
                                    methodology
                                </a>
                                <br />
                                <a href="https://hbr.org/" target="_blank">
                                    <sup>2</sup>Harvard Business Review on
                                    Training Effectiveness
                                </a>
                                <br />
                                <a href="#" target="_blank">
                                    <sup>3</sup>Luis Fernandez - Wow Deck's CEO
                                    &amp; Founder
                                </a>
                                <br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.kirkpatrickpartners.com/"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >
                                    <sup>4</sup>Kirkpatrick's Four Levels of
                                    Training Evaluation
                                </a>
                                <br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en.html"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >
                                    <sup>5</sup>Bersin by Deloitte Research
                                </a>
                                <br />
                                <a
                                    href="https://www.alleninteractions.com/resources/book/michaels-guide-to-elearning"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >
                                    <sup>6</sup>Michael Allen's e-learning
                                    principles
                                </a>
                                <br />
                                <a href="https://www.td.org/" target="_blank">
                                    <sup>7</sup>ASTD (Association for Talent
                                    Development) Reports
                                </a>
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="paragraph-2 bold-text-13">
                        <strong class="bold-text-13">
                            With clear, engaging, and impactful communication
                            tools and training materials, we help you bridge the
                            gap between strategy creation and execution—turning
                            your vision into real, measurable results.
                        </strong>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

